WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.280
the source mentions a maximum conversation

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.200
lifetime of 24 hours.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.240
Yes. The built -in ontology agent's

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.180
conversation history only lasts within

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.680
your current browser session.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.460
Wait, really? If you refresh the

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.460
page, close the browser tab or

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.079
hit the 24 hour mark, that

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:18.400
entire conversational history is permanently

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.120
gone. So under no circumstances should

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.280
a team use the chat window

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.060
as their permanent knowledge repository

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.300
or decision log?

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.720
Absolutely not. The chat is strictly

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.120
an ephemeral scratch pad.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.480
The durable, permanent knowledge must

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.960
be saved in the ontology definitions

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:33.660
themselves,
